# Phase 18 admin header visibility and inherited lo — 2026-10-18 18:29 UTC

- Branch: `phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure`.
- Pinned Java 5.5.1 API inventories confirm that
  `QueryConsumeTimeSpanRequestHeader`, `GetTopicStatsInfoRequestHeader`,
  `DeleteTopicRequestHeader`, `DeleteTopicFromNamesrvRequestHeader`, and
  `DeleteSubscriptionGroupRequestHeader` expose no public fields. Rust fields
  are crate-private; Java-mapped accessors and compile-fail guards were added.
- Source review found `QueryConsumeTimeSpanRequestHeader` extends
  `TopicRequestHeader`; Rust previously omitted its inherited nullable `lo`.
  Rust encode/decode, the Java typed-header fixture, and the header-validation
  matrix now cover `lo=true`. Query-admin API inventory fixture SHA-256:
  `6e92e3d073dcb3b13abbc9c93b94955fd306a5b47576b5c8c52c472a7f668655`.
- Code commit: `3b475951 fix(protocol): align admin request header visibility`.

